// One question the Design settings panel asks Rust: whether a control the Simple interface hides
// holds a value other than its default. The panel (`components/editor_design_settings.slint`)
// uses it to show the one-line note "Some advanced settings are in use". The rule and its tests
// are in Rust: `gui::editor::design_settings_model`.
export global DesignSettingsModel {
    // In this order: the RI Override text, the Extra Header Lines text, the Footnotes text, the
    // Gear Ref. Angle text, the five Printed Proportions texts joined into one string, and the
    // Mirror switch. `true` when any of them is off its default (an empty field, an angle of
    // zero, Mirror off). The Simple interface hides all of them and they still apply.
    pure callback advanced_in_use(string, string, string, string, string, bool) -> bool;
}
